      "body": "Loading an NVFP4 (compressed-tensors) checkpoint on XPU fails at engine init with \"Failed to find a kernel that can implement the NVFP4 linear layer. Reasons:\" and an empty reason list, because _POSSIBLE_NVFP4_KERNELS has CUDA and ROCM entries but no XPU entry, leaving the candidate list empty.\r\n\r\nAdd PlatformEnum.XPU: [EmulationNvFp4LinearKernel], mirroring the existing ROCM entry. The MoE side already auto-selects the EMULATION backend, so no change is needed there.\r\n\r\nEmulation dequantizes FP4 to the activation dtype per forward — a compatibility path, not a performance path — but it makes NVFP4 checkpoints runnable on XPU.\r\n\r\nValidated serving DiffusionGemma-26B-A4B-it-NVFP4 on 4x Intel Arc Pro B70.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
